# --- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/

# Container build-time inputs copied from tools/ (see make test-image)
containers/test/requirements.txt
containers/test/requirements-dev.txt
.coverage
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/

# --- Virtualenv / envs -----------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- Models (never commit large binaries / downloads) ----------------
*.gguf
*.gguf.lock
*.incomplete

# --- Runtime logs written by the tools ---------------------------------
.run.log
*.progress.log

# --- OS / editor --------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Secrets -------------------------------------------------------------
# Real secrets live in `.env`, which is NEVER committed. `.env.example` is a
# committed template documenting the keys (no real values).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# local watch-loop runtime state (host crontab prompt + logs); never commit
.watchloop/
.ci-home/

# --- Artifacts the bots write at the repo root ---------------------------
# Every bot leg writes its run input here: the dispatcher writes issue.md for the agent
# to read, the triage leg writes triage.md (its verdict), the refiner writes
# refine-in.md / refine.md, the implementer writes pr-body.md (the PR description it owes),
# and the outcome step writes comment.md. They are run inputs, never repo content, and
# `git add -A` in a bot run (or in an agent session) would otherwise commit them.
#
# This list is the WHOLE set, and it is enforced with real git by
# tests/test_bot_scratch_ignored.py: a new run input without a line here reds
# `make test-unit`. Do not answer the gap with a `git reset -- <file>` in a workflow —
# that denylist is what shipped a triage verdict as an "implementation" (issue #427).
issue.md
triage.md
refine-in.md
refine.md
comment.md
pr-body.md

# A bot leg's captured agent stream (the `$(call scrubbed_run,…)` seam, issue #359) and its
# REDACTED copy. The raw file is never printed and never uploaded — the scrubbed one is the
# run artifact — and neither belongs in the tree.
hermes-run.log
hermes-run.scrubbed.log

# The host pre-fetch's evidence for the picked issue (issue #380): fetched/index.md plus the text of
# each URL. Written by the refiner leg before the agent runs, read by the agent, never committed —
# it is a snapshot of the outside world at one moment, not a fact about this repository.
fetched/
